EXT. SKI JUMP TOWER - TOP PLATFORM - DAWN

Wind whips the flags. Below, a white ramp falls away to a snowy outrun and a ribbon of crowd.

COACH LARS EKBERG, 50s, fur-trimmed parka, stands behind the jumper with a radio in his fist.

MIKA SAARINEN, 20s, in a skin-tight suit and goggles, sits on the starting bar. Her knees tremble.

OFFICIAL YEVGENY MARKOV, 40s, in an orange vest, hunches over a clipboard and a wind gauge.

LARS
Wind's shifting.

MIKA
Is it going to be okay?

YEVGENY
(to Lars, low)
Eight metres a second. Gusting.

LARS
(to Mika)
It's fine. You've done worse.

MIKA
I haven't.

LARS
You've jumped in a blizzard.

MIKA
I fell in a blizzard.

LARS
You landed in a blizzard.

YEVGENY
(to the radio)
Gate open on my word.

MIKA
Coach, I can't feel my hands.

LARS
Good. Then they can't shake.

YEVGENY
(to the whole tower)
Silence on the platform, please.

Everyone is still. Wind. A raven calls.

LARS
(muttering)
Come on, girl. Come on.

YEVGENY
Go.

Mika pushes off. The ramp swallows her. A hiss of ice. A scream from the crowd, then a roar.

Lars drops the radio. Presses his gloved fists to his mouth.

YEVGENY (CONT'D)
(into the radio, shaky)
She landed. She stood it up.

Lars laughs. Tears freeze on his beard.
